    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i need some help troubleshooting a sublimation issue. we've been running heat transfers for polyester blends but the color vibrancy is way lower than it should be and the edges look blurry. we are currently at 200c for 40 seconds with 4 bar of pressure. any idea what might be causing the poor transfer or the bleeding around the edges?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Lower color vibrancy and blurry edges often suggest an issue with heat application or material preparation. Try slightly increasing the heat temperature or extending the pressing time to ensure full curing of the ink, as polyester blends can be finicky. Also, confirm that your sublimation transfer paper is properly primed and that the polyester blend is pre-pressed with a release agent if the item has a heavier material component.",
      "source": "target",
